# followup-js-math

## native/core/crates/mixdog-js/Cargo.toml

In [dependencies], add the already-cached workspace dependency:

rand = { workspace = true }

The workspace already defines rand = "0.9"; cached sources include 0.9.3 and 0.9.5.
Root owns lock/hakari regeneration. No new crate/package was downloaded.
Production random consumes rand's thread-local entropy-backed generator and applies
V8 RandomNumberGenerator::ToDouble exactly (52 bits, exponent insertion then -1).
The separate Node process's isolate state, seed and refill-cache order are not
observable through the Math.random API and are not reproduced. No weak/time seed.

## Exported APIs (math.rs already re-exports its owned modules)

pub fn abs(x: f64) -> f64;
pub fn floor(x: f64) -> f64;
pub fn ceil(x: f64) -> f64;
pub fn sqrt(x: f64) -> f64;
pub fn acos(x: f64) -> f64;
pub fn asin(x: f64) -> f64;
pub fn atan(x: f64) -> f64;
pub fn atan2(y: f64, x: f64) -> f64;
pub fn sin(x: f64) -> f64;
pub fn cos(x: f64) -> f64;
pub fn tan(x: f64) -> f64;
pub fn random() -> f64;

atan2 follows JavaScript's positional order (first vertical, second horizontal).
The formula leaf's local with_random_sample hook does not need a shared override.
No number.rs/lib.rs/Value changes are included.

## Sources, licenses and verification

Pinned source: official nodejs/node tag v22.20.0, deps/v8/src/base/ieee754.cc.
Installed oracle: Node22.20.0, V8 12.4.254.21-node.33, Windows x64.
The unmodified downloaded source, V8 LICENSE, math-random.cc and
random-number-generator.h are retained under mixdog-js/src/math/reference/;
the fixture manifest records their SHA-256 hashes. Sun's permissive notice is
preserved in each adapted Rust module, and V8's BSD notice is in LICENSE.v8.
Only these authoritative source/license files were downloaded.

No std/libm transcendental fallback: inverse.rs is the fdlibm rational reduction,
trig.rs is the original kernels, reduction.rs retains the 24-bit multiprecision
2/pi convolution, recomputation and summation order for all finite f64 inputs.
The reduction kernel specializes prec=2, its sole caller in V8's binary64 trig.
sqrt uses correctly rounded hardware IEEE arithmetic, as the V8 source does.
NaN payload/sign is preserved explicitly where Windows V8 exposes it, including
the MSVC signaling NaN returned for acos/asin domain errors. These payload bits
are oracle-specific, while all NaNs have the same ECMAScript numeric semantics.
The existing ln negative-domain branch now uses that same signaling NaN (including
negative-sign NaN inputs), and existing min/max return V8's negative canonical
quiet NaN on any NaN input. Their finite algorithms are unchanged. Root requested
these corrections after the strict descriptive-statistics twin exposed them.
The new golden includes log/min/max, so these are not exempted from bit checks.

Index native/core/fixtures/js-math-primitives/MANIFEST.json in the root fixture
index with its existing schema. Recorder --write regenerates only this set;
without --write it prints the deterministic recording to stdout.

After applying the dependency, root runs offline cargo test/clippy for mixdog-js,
including tests/math_primitives_v8.rs and the pre-existing math_v8 regression test.
This worker ran source-table comparisons, rustfmt parsing and bounded Node recording;
no cargo, Rust build/test, applications or real profiles were executed.

Recorded coverage: 56,919 exact-bit calls, including random input bit patterns,
all three argument-reduction ranges, largest finite values, subnormals,
adjacent values around kernel/reduction thresholds and multiples of pi/2,
inverse-domain boundaries, atan2 quadrants and exponent-ratio boundaries,
signed zero, infinities, quiet/signaling NaNs with differing signs/payloads.
The recording also checks 4,096 Node random outputs lie on the 52-bit grid and
inside [0,1). Rust has both sample-invariant tests and deterministic conversion
endpoint tests, without probabilistic distribution thresholds.
Golden SHA256: 9ac137abc439131a7af50a3b65d9a3c1b30809fa5ecc60734fe0dd49090cfc02.
